2321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T15:47:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T15:47:00Z","body":"Since this is a hidden feature, can you add some documentation for it in the editor?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508061542/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508179998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99838#issuecomment-2508179998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99838","id":2508179998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Vf8oe","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T17:19:35Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T17:19:41Z","body":"> Love this! Does this also work when drag-dropping from the FileSystem?\r\n\r\nThis currently doesn't apply to either drag-and-dropping onto an object in the 3D viewport, or drag-and-dropping onto a material property in the inspector. It only applies to drag-and-dropping onto a texture property in a material resource in the inspector.\r\n\r\nI remember editing the drag-and-drop code at some point, so maybe it should be feasible to implement.\r\n\r\n> Since this is a hidden feature, can you add some documentation for it in the editor?\r\n\r\nDone.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508179998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508218797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99838#issuecomment-2508218797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99838","id":2508218797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VgGGt","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T18:02:54Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T18:02:54Z","body":"> It only applies to drag-and-dropping onto a texture property in a material resource in the inspector.\r\n\r\nPerfect! That's what I meant! :)\r\n\r\n> ... so maybe it should be feasible to implement.\r\n\r\nI assume here you mean drag dropping a single texture onto a meshinstance or material property, and it setting up a StandarMaterial3D/ORM for you with the complete textureset?\r\n\r\nIf that's the case, I assume it would be a unique material every time? (Seems like a hard problem to solve otherwise)\r\nConsidering that, I imagine it would lead to users who are not entirely familiar with this behavior finding themselves in a situation where they've dragged-and-dropped the same texture onto various meshes in a scene, assuming it would apply the same material. I imagine there are performance drawbacks to that, compared to having a single resource that's re-used, but even just considering UX it would probably not be the most intuitive.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508218797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508245706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99838#issuecomment-2508245706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99838","id":2508245706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VgMrK","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T18:17:03Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T18:18:41Z","body":"Sounds neat but please not as a hidden miracle.\r\n\r\nMake this texture auto behavior an Editor setting that can be enabled by default but has the option to be disabled.\r\n\r\nSome people get annoyed by the extra clicks of adding textures but I get at least equally annoyed when I have to stare at a frozen Godot due to texture load and add that blocks me from doing anything while firing its selective convenience feature that I dont need. I regularly only want to drag in the albedo texture for a quick model test, not loading all the other textures on purpose because it is so slow. I dont want to rename all those files just to avoid a hidden miracle feature.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508245706/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508278472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99838#issuecomment-2508278472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99838","id":2508278472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VgUrI","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T18:28:33Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T18:28:33Z","body":"> If that's the case, I assume it would be a unique material every time?\r\n\r\nYes, but it's already the case with how the feature works currently.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2508278472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/iss